 bition on view: October 2–December 18\, 2026  For this exhibition\, the
  blueprint is used as both a representational and conceptual departure po
 int. Daniel Luis Martinez uses cyanotype printmaking and mixed-media draw
 ing techniques as a generative process to imagine a speculative home on t
 he CAMi campus. The hybrid drawings and prints featured in the exhibition
  explore the tactile middle-ground of the blueprint as a creative endeavo
 r.  The series employs orthographic conventions typical of architectural 
 drawing sets\, though not as precise instructions for building. Rather\, 
 a layered and loose approach expresses ideas of home as an architectonic 
 language.  Daniel Luis Martinez is a registered architect\, educator\, an
 d co-founder of the multi-disciplinary design studio LAA Office\, which e
 xplores the intersection of landscape\, art\, and architecture. His resea
 rch and creative work investigate the potential of public art to generate
  alternative forms of placemaking. Martinez is Associate Professor and Di
 rector of the IU Eskenazi School's J. Irwin Miller Architecture Program (
 https://architecture.indiana.edu/index.html) in Columbus\, Indiana.  Lear
 n more about the exhibition at the CAMI website (https://camindy.org/exhi
 bitions-all/theblueprint).
