LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Art & a Movie at the Eskenazi Museum: Unfinished Business
DESCRIPTION:Steven Soderbergh's film\, The Christophers\, raises fascinat
 ing questions about authorship\, authenticity\, and value. We prize origi
 nality\, art as the brainchild of a single artist\, completed in a burst 
 of passionate activity. However\, many art objects defy this assumption: 
 they may be products of workshops\; completed in stages or left incomplet
 e\; and/or repaired once or multiple times. Join Dr. Graves to explore ho
 w objects in the museum's collections have been affected by conservators\
 , restorers\, assistants\, and the original artists\, themselves. We'll t
 our the galleries\, examining items ranging from antiquity to only a few 
 decades old. Meet at the museum's 7th St. entrance.  Bio: Jean Graves is 
 the Meier Chair of Education at the Eskenazi Museum of Art. She earned he
 r MA in Art History from Boston University and PhD in Curriculum and Inst
 ruction from Indiana University.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Steven Soder
 bergh's film\, <em>The Christophers</em>\, raises fascinating questions a
 bout authorship\, authenticity\, and value. We prize originality\, art as
  the brainchild of a single artist\, completed in a burst of passionate a
 ctivity. However\, many art objects defy this assumption: they may be pro
 ducts of workshops\; completed in stages or left incomplete\; and/or repa
 ired once or multiple times. Join Dr. Graves to explore how objects in th
 e museum's collections have been affected by conservators\, restorers\, a
 ssistants\, and the original artists\, themselves. We'll tour the galleri
 es\, examining items ranging from antiquity to only a few decades old. Me
 et at the museum's 7<sup>th</sup> St. entrance.</p><p style="font-weight:
  400\;">  Bio: Jean Graves is the Meier Chair of Education at the Eskenaz
 i Museum of Art. She earned her MA in Art History from Boston University 
 and PhD in Curriculum and Instruction from Indiana University.</p>
