LOCATION:McCalla Center\, 525 E. 9th Street\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47408
SUMMARY:McCalla Center Open Gallery Hours
DESCRIPTION:Outfitting IU Athletics: Hoosier Champions                  T
 his exhibit showcases objects from IU's championship teams and athletes\,
  connecting them to historic achievements in the Big Ten and the national
  stage. The items featured in the exhibit are from the IU Athletics Sport
 s Memorabilia Collection and feature photos and videos provided by IU Ath
 letics and Indiana University Archives.                Dates: November 14
 \, 2025 - October 2026          &#160\;                  &#160\;        B
 y Their Own Hands: The Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame!          Founded in
  1974 by the Culture and Ethnic Affairs Guild of the Oakland Museum of Ca
 lifornia\, the Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame began as a film lecture seri
 es and awards ceremony celebrating achievements of Black film industry fi
 gures. When that organization closed\, they donated their materials to IU
 . In collaboration with the IU Black Film Center and Archive\, this exhib
 it features objects from that collection\, including founding documents\,
  costumes\, and handprints of inductees to the Hall of Fame.        Dates
 : September 2025 - December 2026          &#160\;                  &#160\
 ;        Capturing the Campus: T.C. Steele\, Indiana University's First A
 rtist in ResidenceCapturing the Campus pays tribute to renowned Hoosier a
 rtist T.C. Steele. The exhibit honors the century that has passed since h
 is death by showcasing paintings form the artist's residency at IU and ot
 her relevant works. The exhibit will bring together Steele's landscapes f
 rom the IU Public Art and Cultural Heritage Collection and the Indiana St
 ate Museum and Historic Sites' collection\, allowing the holdings of thes
 e two collections to be viewed in one space.        Dates: April 17\, 202
 6 - April 2026          &#160\;        Multipurpose Room          Current
 ly Featuring: The Gift of Collecting: Tina Jernigan          Jernigan was
  a passionate supporter of both Indiana University and the arts. She dona
 ted artworks to the IU Public Art and Cultural Heritage Collection upon h
 er passing in 2024. With funding provided by Jernigan\, Public Art profes
 sionally framed\, hung\, and preserved these pieces for this exhibit in t
 he McCalla Building and for future installations on campus.&#160\;       
  Dates: July 2026-July 2027&#160\;  &#160\;  &#160\;  &#160\;
