SUMMARY:Eiteljorg Artist In Residence Visiting Lecture: Susan Charlesworth
DESCRIPTION:12-1 p.m. Lunch\, Martin Commons\, second floor1–2 p.m. Art
 ist talk\, Learn more about Susan's artistic journey\, creative philosoph
 y\, and evolving practice\, followed by an open Q+A session\, Martin Comm
 ons\, second floor2–4 p.m. Enjoy hands-on artist programming and a rare
  look at selected objects from the museum's collections.  Susan Charleswo
 rth is an award-winning basket weaver who first began weaving in 2005\, w
 hen she entered her baskets into the Choctaw Nation Annual Labor Day Fest
 ival and Art Show. Susan has continued to receive awards at multiple Nati
 ve art markets\, including the Eiteljorg Indian Market &amp\; Festival. S
 usan is a retired CNA and social service consultant with a master's degre
 e in social work and an avid volunteer with the Alzheimer's Association. 
 She now serves as an Alzheimer's Association Community Educator in Indian
 apolis.All of these activities are free and open to the public. This prog
 ram is co-organized by the IU First Nations Educational and Cultural Cent
 er and the Eskenazi Museum of Art\, with support from the Eiteljorg Museu
 m of American Indians and Western Art.
