DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261124
LOCATION:The Contemporary Art Museum of Indianapolis
GEO:39.72915;-86.138756
SUMMARY:Daniel Luis Martinez: The Blueprint | Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Opening reception: Friday\, October 2\, 2026\, 6–10pm  Exhi
 bition on view: October 2–December 18\, 2026  For this exhibition\, the
  blueprint is used as both a representational and conceptual departure po
 int. Daniel Luis Martinez uses cyanotype printmaking and mixed-media draw
 ing techniques as a generative process to imagine a speculative home on t
 he CAMi campus. The hybrid drawings and prints featured in the exhibition
  explore the tactile middle-ground of the blueprint as a creative endeavo
 r.  The series employs orthographic conventions typical of architectural 
 drawing sets\, though not as precise instructions for building. Rather\, 
 a layered and loose approach expresses ideas of home as an architectonic 
 language.  Daniel Luis Martinez is a registered architect\, educator\, an
 d co-founder of the multi-disciplinary design studio LAA Office\, which e
 xplores the intersection of landscape\, art\, and architecture. His resea
 rch and creative work investigate the potential of public art to generate
  alternative forms of placemaking. Martinez is Associate Professor and Di
 rector of the IU Eskenazi School's J. Irwin Miller Architecture Program (
 https://architecture.indiana.edu/index.html) in Columbus\, Indiana.  Lear
 n more about the exhibition at the CAMI website (https://camindy.org/exhi
 bitions-all/theblueprint).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Opening reception: Friday\, Octob
 er 2\, 2026\, 6–10pm<br />  Exhibition on view</strong>: October 2–De
 cember 18\, 2026</p><p>  For this exhibition\, the blueprint is used as b
 oth a representational and conceptual departure point. Daniel Luis Martin
 ez uses cyanotype printmaking and mixed-media drawing techniques as a gen
 erative process to imagine a speculative home on the CAMi campus. The hyb
 rid drawings and prints featured in the exhibition explore the tactile mi
 ddle-ground of the blueprint as a creative endeavor.</p><p>  The series e
 mploys orthographic conventions typical of architectural drawing sets\, t
 hough not as precise instructions for building. Rather\, a layered and lo
 ose approach expresses ideas of home as an architectonic language.</p><p>
   Daniel Luis Martinez is a registered architect\, educator\, and co-foun
 der of the multi-disciplinary design studio LAA Office\, which explores t
 he intersection of landscape\, art\, and architecture. His research and c
 reative work investigate the potential of public art to generate alternat
 ive forms of placemaking. Martinez is Associate Professor and Director of
  the IU Eskenazi School's <a class="external" href="https://architecture.
 indiana.edu/index.html">J. Irwin Miller Architecture Program</a> in Colum
 bus\, Indiana.</p><p>  Learn more about the exhibition at the <a class="e
 xternal" href="https://camindy.org/exhibitions-all/theblueprint">CAMI web
 site</a>.</p>
