SUMMARY:Miller Architecture Program Virtual Info Session: Crafting Your A
 pplication + Program Director Q&A
DESCRIPTION:Today's 60-minute Virtual Information Session will offer guid
 ance on crafting your application and an opportunity to interact with and
  pose questions to Miller Program Director Daniel Martinez.  The J. Irwin
  Miller Master of Architecture program is a three-year in-residence progr
 am\, with a two-year advanced placement track possible for students who h
 old a B.Arch from a NAAB-accredited institution or regional equivalent. W
 ith our twin studios approach\, students take visual art course alongside
  architectural studios to develop their style of architectural design. Th
 e three-year program welcome applicants from a variety of educational and
  career backgrounds.
