X-SOURCE:IU Eskenazi School of Art, Architecture + Design
DTSTART:20261210T150000Z
DTEND:20261210T170000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Light and Chemistry (AM Session)
DESCRIPTION:Through hands-on experiments with viewfinders\, pinhole camer
 as\, and cyanotype photograms\, students will discover how photography ca
 n document history\, reflect change\, and draw inspiration from nature. F
 rom framing a scene to harnessing the power of sunlight\, we'll investiga
 te how images are made and what they can communicate. Join us to experime
 nt\, observe\, and create your own light-powered photographs!  Program de
 signed by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12.Know Befo
 re You Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor 
 of the museum at 10 am. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before e
 xploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our proje
 ct\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our 
 own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcom
 e. Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one a
