BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Eskenazi School of Art, Architecture + Design
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
LOCATION:Four locations on the Bloomington campus
SUMMARY:Mathematics as a Medium: Art\, Practice\, and Inquiry | Symposium
DESCRIPTION:This symposium&#160\;seeks to redefine the genre of mathemati
 cal art\, welcome an international cohort of its practitioners\, and iden
 tify IUB as a leading site for interdisciplinary dialogue between mathema
 tics and the arts.  Organized by Eskenazi School Associate Professor of I
 nterior Design Jiangmei Wu\, who also curated the exhibition\, and Profes
 sor of Mathematics Kevin Pilgrim\, the symposium starts Friday\, January 
 15 at noon and continues through Saturday afternoon.  Over three keynotes
 \, thematic panels\, and workshops\, participating artists\, designers\, 
 mathematicians\, and scholars will explore mathematics as an active mediu
 m of creative practice and create a shared space for exchange among disci
 plines.Visit here for more information about the exhibition. (https://esk
 enazi.indiana.edu/exhibitions/grunwald-gallery/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-m
 edium.html)Visit here for the symposium schedule. (https://eskenazi.india
 na.edu/events/special-events/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium-symposium.ht
 ml)This project was supported by Indiana University's Presidential Arts a
 nd Humanities Program\; the Office for Research Development\, Indiana Uni
 versity Research\; and also at Indiana University Bloomington: Eskenazi S
 chool of Art\, Architecture + Design\; Department of Mathematics\; and Lu
 ddy School of Informatics\, Computing and Engineering Artificial Intellig
 ence Center (LAIC).
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This symposium&#160\;seeks to redefine 
 the genre of mathematical art\, welcome an international cohort of its pr
 actitioners\, and identify IUB as a leading site for interdisciplinary di
 alogue between mathematics and the arts.</p><p class="p1">  Organized by 
 Eskenazi School Associate Professor of Interior Design Jiangmei Wu\, who 
 also curated the exhibition\, and Professor of Mathematics Kevin Pilgrim\
 , the symposium starts Friday\, January 15 at noon and continues through 
 Saturday afternoon.</p><p class="p1">  Over three keynotes\, thematic pan
 els\, and workshops\, participating artists\, designers\, mathematicians\
 , and scholars will explore mathematics as an active medium of creative p
 ractice and create a shared space for exchange among disciplines.</p><p c
 lass="p1"><a href="https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/exhibitions/grunwald-gall
 ery/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
 Visit here for more information about the exhibition.</a></p><p class="p1
 "><a href="https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/events/special-events/upcoming/20
 27-01-15-math-medium-symposium.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit
  here for the symposium schedule.</a></p><p class="p1"><em>This project w
 as supported by Indiana University's Presidential Arts and Humanities Pro
 gram\; the Office for Research Development\, Indiana University Research\
 ; and also at Indiana University Bloomington: Eskenazi School of Art\, Ar
 chitecture + Design\; Department of Mathematics\; and Luddy School of Inf
 ormatics\, Computing and Engineering Artificial Intelligence Center (LAIC
 ).</em></p>
