BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Eskenazi School of Art, Architecture + Design
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270213
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270214
LOCATION:Fine Arts Building\, 1201 East 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
GEO:39.169084;-86.518997
SUMMARY:Mathematics as a Medium | Exhibition
DESCRIPTION:Exhibition Opening Reception: January 15\, 6:30–8:30 pmExhi
 bition Dates: January 15–March 6Symposium Dates: January 15–16  Curat
 ed by Associate Professor of Interior Design in the Eskenazi School of Ar
 t\, Architecture + Design Jiangmei Wu\, the exhibition "Mathematics as a 
 Medium" opening Friday\, January 15 at Indiana University's Grunwald Gall
 ery of Art complements a symposium January 15 and 16 convening many of th
 e exhibitors with counterparts from across the international mathematical
  art community. Over three keynotes\, thematic panels\, and workshops\, p
 articipating artists\, designers\, mathematicians\, and scholars will exp
 lore mathematics as an active medium of creative practice and create a sh
 ared space for exchange among disciplines.  The coordinated events seek t
 o usher in a broader understanding of the relationship between mathematic
 s and art. Proceeding from the proposition that mathematics is a medium�
 �such as paint\, stone\, or sound—through which artists and designers c
 reate and cultures express themselves\, the exhibition and symposium are 
 designed more broadly to redefine mathematics as a living\, generative pr
 actice that shapes how we think\, make\, and experience the world.Visit h
 ere for more information about the exhibition. (https://eskenazi.indiana.
 edu/exhibitions/grunwald-gallery/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium.html)Vis
 it here for the symposium schedule. (https://eskenazi.indiana.edu/events/
 special-events/upcoming/2027-01-15-math-medium-symposium.html)This projec
 t was supported by Indiana University's Presidential Arts and Humanities 
 Program\; the Office for Research Development\, Indiana University Resear
 ch\; and also at Indiana University Bloomington: Eskenazi School of Art\,
  Architecture + Design\; Department of Mathematics\; and Luddy School of 
 Informatics\, Computing and Engineering Artificial Intelligence Center (L
 AIC).
