 anuary 15–16</p><p class="p1">  Curated by Associate Professor of Inter
 ior Design in the Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design Jiangmei
  Wu\, the exhibition "Mathematics as a Medium" opening Friday\, January 1
 5 at Indiana University's Grunwald Gallery of Art complements a symposium
  January 15 and 16 convening many of the exhibitors with counterparts fro
 m across the international mathematical art community. Over three keynote
 s\, thematic panels\, and workshops\, participating artists\, designers\,
  mathematicians\, and scholars will explore mathematics as an active medi
 um of creative practice and create a shared space for exchange among disc
 iplines.</p><p class="p1">  The coordinated events seek to usher in a bro
 ader understanding of the relationship between mathematics and art. Proce
 eding from the proposition that mathematics is a medium—such as paint\,
  stone\, or sound—through which artists and designers create and cultur
 es express themselves\, the exhibition and symposium are designed more br
 oadly to redefine mathematics as a living\, generative practice that shap
 es how we think\, make\, and experience the world.</p><p><a href="https:/
 /eskenazi.indiana.edu/exhibitions/grunwald-gallery/upcoming/2027-01-15-ma
